meta {
  name: DeleteLijnReleasesReservation
  type: http
  seq: 83
}

delete {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/web/bon/{{deleteReleaseBonnr}}/lijn/{{deleteReleaseLijnnr}}
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  X-Auth-Token: {{authToken}}
  Accept: application/json
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.status: eq deleted
}

docs {
  bon-auto-reservering design doc section 6 - deletes the auto-reserved BOM
  bonlijn created by DeleteLijnReleasesReservationCreateLijn. Per the
  design, this must release the pending reservation from BOTH
  artikel.besteld-kl (top-level article) AND its BOM sub-component
  artikel.pbesteld-kl (via
  Luna.BusinessLogic.BonBE:ReleaseReservationForLijn /
  ApplyBomReservationDelta), and delete every bonlijn_productie row
  created for this line. The besteld-kl/pbesteld-kl release itself is not
  independently observable through the documented HTTP contract (no
  exposed GET on artikel's reservation fields) - confirmed via direct
  ABL/DB query during backend-coder implementation. The bonlijn_productie
  cleanup IS independently observable - see
  Bon/Productie/List.bru (GET .../lijn/{lijnnr}/productie) returning an
  empty items array for {{deleteReleaseLijnnr}} after this delete, same
  verification approach as AnnuleerCleansUpProductieRows.bru. Requires
  {{deleteReleaseBonnr}}/{{deleteReleaseLijnnr}} (run
  "DeleteLijnReleasesReservationCreateLijn" first).
}
